(*
expect:
ok
expect-runtime-fail: not a value
*)
(* T-B.6 variant — a plain heap object of a class DEFINED IN THIS TEST MODULE
   (no isValue override) nested deep inside an otherwise-valid List tree is
   `not a value` at construction, same per-element-at-every-depth validation
   as 16/16c/16d.

   CAUTION verified before landing (per the brief): this assumes a user heap
   class inherits Kernel Object's `valueRank = -1` via NORMAL vtable
   delegation. Confirmed in ns_compile_oevm.py's compile_class: any rootless
   (no explicit superclass) class delegates its vtable to Vtable_Kernel_Object,
   so `Thing new valueRank` dispatches all the way up to Object's `^ -1` like
   any other user class. The Task-2 "no delegation" finding is unrelated — it
   was about BUILTIN vtables (String, Integer, ...) hardcoding a NULL
   delegate, not about classes the app/test module itself defines. So this
   lands as a plain (rankOf: -> platform valueRank: answers -1 for "other
   heap" -> falls back to `v valueRank` -> Object's -1) `not a value` crash,
   no DNU. *)
class MutableBoundaryUserObject packageUsing: manifest = () (
class Thing = () (
) : (
)
public main: platform args: args = (
  | L |
  L:: platform List.
  'ok' out.
  L with: 1 with: (L with: 2 with: (L with: 3 with: Thing new)).
  'unreached' out.
)
) : (
)
